            "body": "Have you seen #195?\r\n\r\n> I map `i` to `l` and `k` to `i`. So when setup mini.ai mappings below\r\n\r\nThe suggested solution to deal with different keyboard layout is with `langmap`. Try adding `vim.o.langmap = 'ki,il'` to your config and have `require('mini.ai').setup()` with default mappings. It should work as expected.",
