            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> langmap is a way switch between language, not keyboard layout. Using langmap will be causing more confusion, for example,\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> vim.o.langmap = 'ki,il'\r\n> vim.o.langremap = false\r\n> vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>sk\", ...)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> when you typed sk, `k` will treat as `i`\r\n\r\nOne solution is to make `<Leader>si` mapping and type `<Leader>sk`. Not ideal, but doable.\r\n\r\nI think this is the best it could get here. Deleting and then reenabling mappings can not be a solution here.",
